00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.713
Hell of a job, Willie.

00:20:56.713 --> 00:20:58.630
Could you have written
a more storybook ending

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:00.910
for your two games over here?

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.680
I mean, it was pretty
special, for sure,

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:05.380
to get that OT winner there.

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:08.170
Just playing the games
and being with my family

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:10.790
and showing the guys.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.132
Those three things were special.

00:21:12.132 --> 00:21:12.840
Had a lot of fun.

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:13.890
City was great.

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:14.937
Atmosphere was great.

00:21:14.937 --> 00:21:17.520
You know, I think it was just a
cool kind of little experience

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.650
that you got to enjoy
with your teammates.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.270
4 points on this trip, OK?

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:22.590
Four important points.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.450
Find ways to get the job done.

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:25.920
That feels good going home.

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:27.233
Bert, hang that thing out.

00:21:27.233 --> 00:21:27.900
Get out of here.

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.380
Great stuff, boys.

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:33.160
Small, Tone, PK [MUTED]
great job tonight.

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.980
But this guy runs
this city, man.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.850
Go home and [MUTED]
keep this thing going.

00:21:47.418 --> 00:21:48.960
That's so much fun,
you know, getting

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:51.750
to play in a different barn,
and it's a pretty fun atmosphere

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:53.430
when you can, you
know, bring four teams

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:55.650
to an event like this.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:57.330
I think it's special
for everybody.

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:00.720
The museums, the culture, the
atmosphere, and the city-- it's

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:03.872
such a beautiful city, and
the people are so welcoming.

00:22:03.872 --> 00:22:04.830
Raymond in with a shot.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.480
He scores!

00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:07.860
A good experience for him.

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.740
It's one of the big
reasons we're here--

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:12.127
to build the game a little bit.

00:22:12.127 --> 00:22:14.460
And just good players are
going to be a big part of what

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:15.760
we're doing going forward.

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:16.510
It's been awesome.

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:18.420
I mean, the whole
week has been great.

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:19.350
So, yeah.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:20.980
We've been playing
good hockey too.

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:22.045
So, it's a good trip.

00:22:22.045 --> 00:22:23.670
A lot of great memories
in the process.

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:24.670
A lot of great memories.

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:26.640
You know, Forsberg,
Brannström, guys

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:28.620
like that who got to come
back, family friends,

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:29.550
play in front of them.

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:31.717
Very cool experience for
all these Swedish guys that

00:22:31.717 --> 00:22:33.300
come here and be
able to play in front

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:34.760
of their family and friends.

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:37.260
The connection with
Sweden and Swedes

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:39.060
is strong with the Maple Leafs.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:41.580
That gives you a
sense of perspective,

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:44.790
of folks like Salming and
Sundin and those that have

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:46.960
come before our current crop.

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:49.980
It had a lot of people,
friends, family at the games.

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:51.960
I mean, my grandma that
hasn't seen me play

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:55.368
live before, I think some
of my aunts and uncles

00:22:55.368 --> 00:22:56.910
that haven't seen
me play their live.

00:22:56.910 --> 00:22:58.380
Was lots of fun to
have him out there.

00:22:58.380 --> 00:23:00.450
Just enjoy the time that
we had before I headed

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:02.158
home I think was very
special, and that's

00:23:02.158 --> 00:23:03.800
something I'll remember.

